            <ArticleTitle>Pericardial tamponade and coronary sinus thrombosis associated with central venus catheterization.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1154-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the rare occurrence of fatal cardiac tamponade due to coronary sinus and right atrial thrombosis associated with central venous catheterization. The clinical course was extremely rapid, with death occurring a few minutes after the acute clinical event. Other causes of acute cardiac tamponade were ruled out by the postmortem studies.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
